    "explanation": "To both parties: the trip's own telemetry establishes a route deviation, and the refund is arithmetic. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00509) records 17.14 km driven against the booked optimal of 9.6 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00509) — an excess of 7.54 km, 78.5% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass (above 20% and above 0.8 km) and the excess also exceeds 50%, so the deviation is established and material. The trace figure governs; the trip record's rounded 17.1 km is not used for the threshold test. Running POL-RD-02 on the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00509): charged_total is SGD 26.39; recomputed_fare = (3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 9.6 km + 0.28 x 14.0 min) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from the fare breakdown, + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP/tolls + 0 surcharge + 0 waiting time - 0 promo = SGD 15.72. The refund is 26.39 - 15.72 = SGD 10.67, rounded up to SGD 10.70. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and 40.4% of the charge, below the 90% that would make it a full refund, so it is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 10.70. Nothing is stacked on top: erp_gantries is empty, tolls, airport surcharge and waiting fee are all nil, and POL-RD-09's anti-double-count rule bars adding any pass-through figure to the 10.70. The driver's conduct check was run and does not fire: deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 150 completed trips in the 90-day window, so POL-RD-06 establishes no pattern, grants no full-refund uplift and produces no conduct referral; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only and was not used. The driver's explanation that the navigation kept re-routing him is an external-cause assertion, tested under POL-RD-13 against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else. No advisory is on file: EV-ADVIS-00509-01 is MISSING with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08; it is discarded and the ruling records that no advisory was on file. Because the driver named no advisory evidence ID, the absence is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so the POL-RD-10(5) escalation the driver's advocate argued for does not fire, and the deviation stands at the measured figure against the booked optimal route. No other POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 (193 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s), trip identifiers match across all three instruments, the timestamps do not conflict or run backwards, and the refund is well within the ceiling. The rider's consequential losses — the missed bus, the replacement ticket and the lost evening — are not a remedy this policy provides; POL-RD-02 makes the refund traceable to fare lines only. The rider's account of being set down at the wrong building also buys no adjustment: the trip record shows no amended pickup or dropoff and no amended optimal route, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run and the booked 9.6 km optimal stands. The rider's recovery is therefore SGD 10.70 and no more.",
